            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_AECUt8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>When we talk about regenerative aquaculture, we're speaking about far more than the farms we partner with. We see aquaculture as part of a living system — one that connects growers, harvesters, distributors, cooks, and everyone who gathers around the table. For something to be truly regenerative, participation is required from every part of the system.</p><p>Showing up to a gathering with an intentionally sourced dish is an offering that reflects your values, your choices, and the networks of relationships you help sustain. When you arrive, you are saying: <em>“I care about where my nourishment comes from, and I care about how I nourish the people around me.”</em></p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
